    "title": "Olivia Rodrigo Begins Next Era with New Song \"drop dead\"",
    "text": "April 17, 2026 | 12:00am ET Olivia Rodrigo’s next era officially begins with her new song, “drop dead,” the first single from her upcoming third album, you seem pretty sad for a girl so in love. Watch the accompanying music video, filmed in the The Palace of Versailles and directed by Petra Collins, below. Update: Read our review of the track here. Rodrigo will likely perform “drop dead” while pulling double duty as the Saturday Night Live host and musical guest on May 2nd. The pop star previously described you seem pretty sad, the follow-up to 2023’s GUTS, as a “creative challenge” because it was written while in a relationship with British actor Louis Partridge. “I realized all my favorite romantic love songs were beautiful because they had a tinge of fear or yearning in them,” Rodrigo explained, adding that she was inspired by the obsession and anxiety of her own romance. you seem pretty sad for a girl so in love is set for release on June 12th via Geffen Records. Pre-orders are ongoing. In gossip news, Rodrigo was reportedly spotted on a date with Geese’s Cameron Winter earlier this week. We'd like to show you notifications for the latest news and updates.",
